29. 【解】（方法一）

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{左端}
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{e^{\frac{\ln(1+\sin2x^2)-2x^2}{x^2}}-1}{x^n}\\
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\ln(1+\sin2x^2)-2x^2}{x^{n+2}}
\quad(e^x-1\sim x)\\
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}
\frac{\frac{4x\cos2x^2}{1+\sin2x^2}-4x}{(n+2)x^{n+1}}\\
&=\frac{4e^2}{n+2}\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\cos2x^2-1-\sin2x^2}{x^n}\\
&=a\ne0.
\end{aligned}
$$

$n=2,\ a=-2e^2$。

（方法二）

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{左端}
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\ln(1+\sin2x^2)-2x^2}{x^{n+2}}\\
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}
\frac{\sin2x^2-\frac{\sin^22x^2}{2}+o(\sin^22x^2)-2x^2}{x^{n+2}}
\qquad（泰勒公式）\\
&=a\ne0.
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\text{所以 }n=2,\ a=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{-\frac{\sin^2(2x^2)}{2}}{x^4}=-2e^2.
$$

（方法三）

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{左端}
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\ln(1+\sin2x^2)-2x^2}{x^{n+2}}\\
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}
\frac{[\ln(1+\sin2x^2)-\sin2x^2]-(2x^2-\sin2x^2)}{x^{n+2}}\\
&=e^2\lim_{x\to0}
\frac{\left[-\frac{1}{2}(\sin2x^2)^2\right]-\left[\frac{1}{6}(2x^2)^3\right]}{x^{n+2}},
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
(x-\ln(1+x))\sim\frac{1}{2}x^2,\quad x-\sin x\sim\frac{1}{6}x^3,
$$

$$
\text{所以 }n=2,\ a=e^2\lim_{x\to0}\frac{-2x^4}{x^4}=-2e^2.
$$

30. 【解】由于 $x\to0$ 时，$ax-\sin x\to0$，且极限 $c$ 不为零，所以当 $x\to0$ 时，

$$
\int_b^x\frac{\ln(1+t^3)}{t}\,dt\to0,
$$

故必有 $b=0$。

由于

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{x\to0}\frac{ax-\sin x}{\int_0^x\frac{\ln(1+t^3)}{t}\,dt}
&=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{a-\cos x}{\frac{\ln(1+x^3)}{x}}\\
&=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{a-\cos x}{x^2}=c\quad(c\ne0),
\end{aligned}
$$

故必有 $a=1$，从而 $c=\frac{1}{2}$。

31. 【解】（方法一）

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{原式}
&=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin^2x-\ln(1+x^2)}{\ln(1+x^2)\sin^2x}\\
&=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin^2x-\ln(1+x^2)}{x^4}\\
&=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{2\sin x\cos x-\frac{2x}{1+x^2}}{4x^3}
\qquad（洛必达法则）\\
&=\frac{1}{4}\lim_{x\to0}\frac{(1+x^2)\sin2x-2x}{x^3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

【注】解本题时一开始就用洛必达法则：

$$
2=\lim_{x\to0}\left(\frac{\sin x}{x^2}+\frac{f(x)}{x}\right)
=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin x+xf(x)}{x^2}
=\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\cos x+f(x)+xf'(x)}{2x}.
$$

似乎也可得到 $f(0)=-1$，但这样做是错误的。其原因是对洛必达法则的条件理解不透。即我们并不知道

$$
\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\cos x+f(x)+f'(x)}{2x}
$$

是否存在。

38.【解】

$$
\frac{\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(2n+1)}{\sqrt{n^6+n^2}}
\leq
\frac{1}{\sqrt{n^6+n}}+\frac{2^2}{\sqrt{n^6+2n}}+\cdots+\frac{n^2}{\sqrt{n^6+n^2}}
$$

$$
\leq
\frac{\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(2n+1)}{\sqrt{n^6+n}},
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(2n+1)}{\sqrt{n^6+n}}
&=\frac{1}{6}\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{n^3\sqrt{\frac{n^6+n}{n^6}}}\\
&=\frac{1}{6}\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\left(1+\frac{1}{n}\right)\left(2+\frac{1}{n}\right)}{\sqrt{1+\frac{1}{n^5}}}\\
&=\frac{1}{6}\cdot\frac{1\times2}{\sqrt{1}}=\frac{1}{3},
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{\frac{1}{6}n(n+1)(2n+1)}{\sqrt{n^6+n^2}}=\frac{1}{3}.
$$

由夹逼定理可得，原极限 $=\frac{1}{3}$.

39.【解】

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\left(
\frac{1}{\sqrt{n^2}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{n^2-1^2}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{\sqrt{n^2-(n-1)^2}}
\right)
&=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\left(
\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-0}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\left(\frac{n-1}{n}\right)^2}}
\right)\\
&=\int_0^1\frac{dx}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}=\frac{\pi}{2}.
\end{aligned}
$$

40.【解】

$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{1}{n}\left[
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}
+\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{2}{n}\right)^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{n}{n}\right)^2}
\right]
&<
\left[
\frac{n+1}{1^2+n^2}
+\frac{n+\frac{1}{2}}{2^2+n^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{n+\frac{1}{n}}{n^2+n^2}
\right]\\
&<
\frac{n+1}{n^2}\left[
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}
+\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{2}{n}\right)^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{n}{n}\right)^2}
\right],
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\left[
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}
+\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{2}{n}\right)^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{n}{n}\right)^2}
\right]
=\int_0^1\frac{1}{1+x^2}\,dx=\frac{\pi}{4},
$$

$$
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n^2}\left[
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}
+\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{2}{n}\right)^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{n}{n}\right)^2}
\right]=0,
$$

$$
\frac{n+1}{n^2}=\frac{1}{n}+\frac{1}{n^2},
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{n+1}{n^2}\left[
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)^2}
+\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{2}{n}\right)^2}
+\cdots+
\frac{1}{1+\left(\frac{n}{n}\right)^2}
\right]
&=\int_0^1\frac{1}{1+x^2}\,dx+0\\
&=\frac{\pi}{4}.
\end{aligned}
$$

35.【解】$\ln(1+\sqrt{2})$.

$$y'=\tan x,$$

$$
s=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\sqrt{1+(\tan x)^2}\,dx
=\int_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}\frac{dx}{\cos x}
=\left.\ln|\sec x+\tan x|\right|_0^{\frac{\pi}{4}}
